      },
      "worked": "\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=\\dfrac{m(1+x)^{m-1}(1-x)^n+n(1+x)^m(1-x)^{n-1}}{(1-x)^{2n}}\\\\f'(x)&=\\dfrac{(1+x)^{m-1}[(m+n)+(n-m)x]}{(1-x)^{n+1}}.\\end{align*}$$\n\n The numerator is zero when $x=-1$ or $x=\\dfrac{m+n}{m-n}$. Since $m$ and $n$ are integers greater than $1$, both values are in the domain $x\\ne1$. Hence both satisfy $f'(x)=0$.",
